## Plan

_Written by `claude-6` (claude, `opus`, strong) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/39893622806)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

The opponent's reply (`simulate_reply_with` in `crates/ai/src/reply.rs`) gets one more step. When the static trader finds no attack worth making, it tries switching each of its units that is in Attack Position and can still switch to Defense Position. It keeps the switch its own `evaluate` likes best, if that beats standing still. Otherwise it ends its turn as before.

A new named constant, `AI_REPLY.defense_switches`, caps the tries per step. Seeded reply tests show a unit with no positive attack switching when `evaluate` prefers Defense, and staying in Attack when it does not. Done means `cargo test -p jackioh-ai` is green and neither the gate smoke nor a paired screen shows a regression.

## Files to touch

| File | Kind | What changes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `crates/ai/src/config.rs` | change | new field `AiReply::defense_switches: i32`, set to `4` in `AI_REPLY` |
| `crates/ai/src/reply.rs` | change | import `Position`; header step 4; `Known` doc; new `fn defense_switch`; its call in `simulate_reply_with`; one comment |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/reply.rs` | change | node count 1 → 2 in `b41_does_not_throw_a_unit_into_a_defense_position_wall_it_cannot_hurt_and_ends_its_turn_instead`; new `mod defense_switch_1696` with 3 tests |
| `crates/ai/README.md` | change | the reply's steps in the `decide` paragraph |
| `docs/polish/3-ai.md` | change | "The rule, one step at a time": new step 4 **Defense**; **End** becomes step 5 |
| `spec/09-architecture.md` | change | one new sentence in §9.9's "The opponent's reply" bullet |

Do not touch:
- `crates/engine` and `crates/cards`.
- `crates/server`, including `tests/fixtures/practice-claim.json`.
- `apps/web`.
